      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "h3"
    },
    {
      "_key": "bpqoqaks0",
      "_type": "block",
      "children": [
        {
          "_key": "bj10ndnaq",
          "_type": "span",
          "marks": [],
          "text": "The tour begins at the Colosseum entrance with skip-the-line access to explore the amphitheater's seating levels and learn about gladiatorial combat lasting up to 100 days. You'll spend approximately 45 minutes inside the Colosseum before moving to the Roman Forum via the connecting entrance. The Forum portion covers 1 hour walking through the Via Sacra, Temple ruins, and political centers of ancient Rome. Standing among the weathered marble columns of the Temple of Caesar, you can see the exact spot where Romans cremated their assassinated leader in 44 BC. The final 45 minutes explores Palatine Hill's imperial palace ruins and terraces, with the total walking distance covering approximately 2 miles across uneven ancient stones."
        }
      ],
      "markDefs": [],
      "style": "normal"
